ine comes only from the fixture regime. Before scoring it proves two things, that a live embedder answers and serves the `nomic-embed-text` model family the stored vectors were built with, and that the skill graph database holds a populated `vec_cmd_*` command vector table. A missing piece exits 2 with a message that names it. |\n73: | `score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Scores captured sessions through the shared session readers. `--summary <run-log> [<run-log>...]` scores every row one or more run logs list, per runtime and arm, and `--runtime <name> --locator '<json>'` scores the one session a locator names. `--row-id <id>` narrows either mode to one row and `--json` prints machine-readable output. Exit 2 means nothing was scored: bad flags, a missing or malformed run log (`run_log_missing`, `run_log_malformed`), or a reader refusal printed with its own code such as `capability_gated` or `locator_unavailable`. |\n74: | `run-command-behaviour.mjs` | Runs one live turn per row and records the locator, exit and changed paths. `--print-argv <runtime>` prints a runtime's argv, `--list <set>` prints a set's row ids, and a run takes `--runtime` with `--set` or repeated `--row-id`, `--out <run-log>`, optional `--arm`, `--fixture` and `--dry-run`. Exit 2 refuses instead of running: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout or unknown row, a set with fewer rows than it needs (`set_short`), a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder (`worktree_dirty`), or a checkout with a git remote (`remote_present`). |\n75: | `command-routing-baseline.json` | Captured command routing numbers that `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` holds the scorer to. |\n76: \n77: ---\n78: \n79: ## 5. CONFIGURATION\n80: \n81: | Setting | Default | Purpose |\n82: |---|---|---|\n83: | sk-code surface | OPENCODE | Applies OpenCode TypeScript, JavaScript, Python, Shell and config conventions. |\n84: | README scope | Direct folder | This file documents this folder, not sibling folders. |\n85: \n86: ---\n87: \n88: ## 6. USAGE EXAMPLES\n89: \n90: **Audit this folder**\n91: \n92: ```text\n93: User request: Check .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy for sk-code and README coverage.\n94: Skill routing: sk-code plus sk-doc.\n95: Expected output: Findings recorded in the 026 audit report.\n96: ```\n97: \n98: **Score captured runs**\n99: \n100: ```bash\n101: node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs \\\n102:   --summary scratch/runs-pre.jsonl scratch/runs-post.jsonl --json\n103: ```\n104: \n105: Exit 2 means no score was produced. A missing or malformed log prints `run_log_missing` or `run_log_malformed`, and a session the reader cannot open prints its own code, such as `capability_gated`.\n106: \n107: **Inspect and run one behaviour turn**\n108: \n109: ```bash\n110: node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs --print-argv claude\n111: node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs \\\n112:   --runtime claude --set chat --out scratch/runs-pre.jsonl --dry-run\n113: ```\n114: \n115: Exit 2 means the run was refused before or during its first prompt: bad flags, an unknown runtime or set, a holdout row, a dirty worktree outside the run log's folder, or a checkout that still has a git remote.\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## 7. TROUBLESHOOTING\n120: \n121: | What You See | Cause | Fix |\n122: |---|---|---|\n123: | README appears stale | Source files changed after this audit | Refresh the structure table and rerun the 026 audit check. |\n124: | Verification command is unclear | Folder is a helper boundary | Use the nearest package or skill-level verification command. |\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: ## 8. RELATED DOCUMENTS\n129: \n130: | Document | Purpose |\n131: |---|---|\n132: | [`system-skill-advisor/SKILL.md`](../../../SKILL.md) | Runtime instructions for the owning skill. |\n133: | [`sk-code/SKILL.md`](../../../../sk-code/SKILL.md) | OpenCode coding standards and verification routing. |\n134: | [`sk-doc skill-readme-template.md`](../../../../sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-readme-template.md) | README structure used for this code README. |"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529872917,"end":1794529874344}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529874368,"sessionID":"ses_e2dafa57effeO4wwa27i0dv11O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d250cdfa0010ATx8CX7N3i6jL","sessionID":"ses_e2dafa57effeO4wwa27i0dv11O","messageID":"msg_1d250bb73001OJbYmkdalxazQl","type":"tool","id":"call_1765d98784bf4b8db8d800e0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"offeredCommand|offeredPolicy|briefDelivered|offerError|offerBackfilled|no_checkout|same_path|holdout|unknown_row|promptFor\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"12:// A failed replay returns null fields plus an offerError, so a backfill over a\n40:function failedOffer(offerError) {\n41:  return { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError };\n51: * @returns {{ offeredCommand: string | null, offeredPolicy: string | null }}\n57:    return { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null };\n61:    offeredCommand: match[0],\n62:    offeredPolicy: policy ? policy[1] : null,\n78: * @returns {{ offeredCommand: string | null, offeredPolicy: string | null, offerError: string | null }}\n127:  return { ...parseOffer(firstLine), offerError: null };\n162:export async function briefDelivered({ runtime, locator, loadSession } = {}) {\n246: * @param {(rowId: string) => string} options.promptFor - Prompt lookup. It\n247: *   refuses an unknown or holdout row by throwing an error with a `code`.\n258:  promptFor,\n260:  brief = briefDelivered,\n264:    return refused('same_path', `${outPath}: the backfill writes a new log`);\n276:      prompts.push(promptFor(row.rowId));\n278:      return refused(error?.code ?? 'unknown_row', error?.message ?? String(error));\n293:    let offer = { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_checkout' };\n317:      offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand ?? null,\n318:      offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,\n319:      offerError: offer.offerError ?? null,\n320:      briefDelivered: delivered,\n321:      offerBackfilled: true,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"12:// A failed replay returns null fields plus an offerError, so a backfill over a\n40:function failedOffer(offerError) {\n41:  return { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError };\n51: * @returns {{ offeredCommand: string | null, offeredPolicy: string | null }}\n57:    return { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null };\n61:    offeredCommand: match[0],\n62:    offeredPolicy: policy ? policy[1] : null,\n78: * @returns {{ offeredCommand: string | null, offeredPolicy: string | null, offerError: string | null }}\n127:  return { ...parseOffer(firstLine), offerError: null };\n162:export async function briefDelivered({ runtime, locator, loadSession } = {}) {\n246: * @param {(rowId: string) => string} options.promptFor - Prompt lookup. It\n247: *   refuses an unknown or holdout row by throwing an error with a `code`.\n258:  promptFor,\n260:  brief = briefDelivered,\n264:    return refused('same_path', `${outPath}: the backfill writes a new log`);\n276:      prompts.push(promptFor(row.rowId));\n278:      return refused(error?.code ?? 'unknown_row', error?.message ?? String(error));\n293:    let offer = { offeredCommand: null, offeredPolicy: null, offerError: 'no_checkout' };\n317:      offeredCommand: offer.offeredCommand ?? null,\n318:      offeredPolicy: offer.offeredPolicy ?? null,\n319:      offerError: offer.offerError ?? null,\n320:      briefDelivered: delivered,\n321:      offerBackfilled: true,\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"offeredCommand|offeredPolicy|briefDelivered|offerError|offerBackfilled|no_checkout|same_path|holdout|unknown_row|promptFor\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529873402,"end":1794529874368}}}}
