{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529908134,"sessionID":"ses_e2dafa57effeO4wwa27i0dv11O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2515297002zn0pqPiQADknPv","sessionID":"ses_e2dafa57effeO4wwa27i0dv11O","messageID":"msg_1d2511fe2001KW74jC0mbSjQZw","type":"tool","id":"call_c0428389801b4915bd7eb66f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ 2>/dev/null; rg -n \"code README|code-folder|Code README\" .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/SKILL.md | head -20","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"assets\nchangelog\nmanual-testing-playbook\nREADME.md\nreferences\nROUTER.md\nscripts\nSKILL.md\n3:description: Author sk-doc folder, code-folder and skill/project READMEs from local evidence.\n42:`sk-doc` routes README authoring here: the request names a README, a folder readme, a code-folder readme or `/create:readme`.\n44:Three artifacts route here: a general README, a code-folder README and a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\n62:3. Draft current-state content only, in the smallest useful shape: a general README (Section 5) or a code-folder README (Section 6).\n75:4. Choose the smallest useful README shape. Use a general README for project, skill, feature and component roots. Use a code-folder README for source-directory orientation.\n80:9. Use technical reference voice for component and code-folder READMEs.\n145:Create a code-folder README when a developer needs local orientation before editing the directory.\n175:The general README format rules at `General README format rules:` above bind code-folder READMEs.\n179:It does not bind code-folder READMEs.\n198:- The code-folder scaffold omits the general blockquote tagline by design. Frontmatter remains optional, and when present it stays before the H1.\n230:- README type is correct. Code folders use the code-folder shape.\n262:- Force Quick Start, Features, FAQ or Troubleshooting into a code-folder README when the folder only needs orientation.\n273:- Use analogies only when they clarify narrative sections. Do not use analogies in component or code-folder READMEs.\n289:- `assets/readme-code-template.md` for the full fillable code-folder scaffold and diagram examples.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"assets\nchangelog\nmanual-testing-playbook\nREADME.md\nreferences\nROUTER.md\nscripts\nSKILL.md\n3:description: Author sk-doc folder, code-folder and skill/project READMEs from local evidence.\n42:`sk-doc` routes README authoring here: the request names a README, a folder readme, a code-folder readme or `/create:readme`.\n44:Three artifacts route here: a general README, a code-folder README and a skill package's `ARCHITECTURE.md`.\n62:3. Draft current-state content only, in the smallest useful shape: a general README (Section 5) or a code-folder README (Section 6).\n75:4. Choose the smallest useful README shape. Use a general README for project, skill, feature and component roots. Use a code-folder README for source-directory orientation.\n80:9. Use technical reference voice for component and code-folder READMEs.\n145:Create a code-folder README when a developer needs local orientation before editing the directory.\n175:The general README format rules at `General README format rules:` above bind code-folder READMEs.\n179:It does not bind code-folder READMEs.\n198:- The code-folder scaffold omits the general blockquote tagline by design. Frontmatter remains optional, and when present it stays before the H1.\n230:- README type is correct. Code folders use the code-folder shape.\n262:- Force Quick Start, Features, FAQ or Troubleshooting into a code-folder README when the folder only needs orientation.\n273:- Use analogies only when they clarify narrative sections. Do not use analogies in component or code-folder READMEs.\n289:- `assets/readme-code-template.md` for the full fillable code-folder scaffold and diagram examples.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"ls .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/ 2>/dev/null; rg -n \\\"code README|code-folder|Code README\\\" .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-readme/SKILL.md | head -20\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529907351,"end":1794529908134}}}}
