{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794529935020,"sessionID":"ses_e2dafa57effeO4wwa27i0dv11O","part":{"partID":"prt_1d251af46001INCwt5nVlzBXcT","sessionID":"ses_e2dafa57effeO4wwa27i0dv11O","messageID":"msg_1d2515db30011TEIGdDphBXmAn","type":"tool","id":"call_386c5be6a53b4a8aaf6696ff","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md","oldString":"| Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. STRUCTURE","newString":"| Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\n\n### Attribution on every run line\n\nEach line a behaviour run appends carries three fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n\n- `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\n- `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\n- `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a record, and `unknown` where no record exists, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\n\nThe offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n\n### Backfill a finished log\n\n`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n\n- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\n- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n\nA line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. STRUCTURE"},"output":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md","patch":"Index: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n===================================================================\n--- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n+++ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\n@@ -59,8 +59,27 @@\n | Folder boundary | Documents direct code files under `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy`. |\n | sk-code alignment | Points reviewers at OpenCode naming, header, error-handling and type-discipline checks. |\n | Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\n \n+### Attribution on every run line\n+\n+Each line a behaviour run appends carries three fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\n+\n+- `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\n+- `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\n+- `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a record, and `unknown` where no record exists, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\n+\n+The offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\n+\n+### Backfill a finished log\n+\n+`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\n+\n+- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\n+- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\n+\n+A line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\n+\n ---\n \n ## 4. STRUCTURE\n \n","status":"modified","additions":19,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md\",\"oldString\":\"| Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. STRUCTURE\",\"newString\":\"| Verification handoff | Records the expected owner and audit packet for follow-up work. |\\n\\n### Attribution on every run line\\n\\nEach line a behaviour run appends carries three fields beside the locator, exit and changed paths:\\n\\n- `offeredCommand` is the slash command the advisor head named, or `null` when the head named none.\\n- `offeredPolicy` is the policy that directly follows that command, one of `run`, `start` or `ask`, or `null` when no policy follows it.\\n- `briefDelivered` says whether the advisor brief reached the session. It is `true` or `false` where the runtime keeps a record, and `unknown` where no record exists, so a gap in the record never reads as a miss.\\n\\nThe offer is a replay of the Claude prompt hook after the turn instead of a copy of the live session head. The head is the only text that names both the command and the policy, and not every runtime keeps it, so `replayOffer` runs the checkout's own hook and records what that checkout would have offered at the time of the run. A replay that finds no hook, a failing hook or a head without an offer writes null fields plus an `offerError` of `hook_missing`, `hook_failed` or `no_head`, so one bad line never aborts a run.\\n\\n### Backfill a finished log\\n\\n`run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill <run-log> --out <new-log>` adds those three fields to a log written before they existed, and a `--backfill` run without `--out` is a usage error that exits 2. The mode refuses with exit 2 and a JSON body holding its `code`:\\n\\n- `same_path` when `--out` resolves to the input log, because the backfill writes a new file.\\n- `holdout_row` or `unknown_row` when the corpus refuses a row id, because every prompt is resolved before the first line is written and a refused row leaves no output file behind.\\n\\nA line whose locator names no checkout keeps null offer fields and `offerError` `no_checkout`, and the rest of the log is still written with `offerBackfilled: true`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. STRUCTURE\"}"},"time":{"start":1794529931078,"end":1794529935020}}}}
